^/\.icons(/|$)
^/\.local/share/icons(/|$)
^/\.themes(/|$)
^/\.local/share/themes(/|$)
# Rule 20 guard: .hermes is a private mutable app-config tree owned by HelmCortex
# (~/HelmCortex/NEXUS/stow/linux/.hermes, deployed via helmstow). It must NEVER be
# folded from DotCortex — a stray all/.hermes once hijacked the ~/.hermes symlink and
# stripped Hermes of its config.yaml + .env. Never let stow fold it again.
^/\.hermes(/|$)
# The mutable Claude settings file is a regular live union. DotCortex and
# HelmCortex merge their own entries; Stow must never claim this exact file.
^/\.claude/settings\.json$
# Sanctuary guest home dirs are managed by sanctuary-enter, not stow.
# They contain absolute symlinks (bind-mount targets into the container) that stow cannot install.
# ~/.local/share/dotcortex/guests/ is a real directory created by sanctuary setup,
# so stow traverses into it and hits these symlinks — ignore the whole subtree.
^/\.local/share/dotcortex/guests(/|$)
# Service lanes run from a root-owned system checkout, never from a home
# (agents-bots-honey.org, "Service lane"): never link them.
^/\.local/share/dotcortex/honey-claude(/|$)
# skill-creator is an absolute symlink into the ductor_bot package tree.
# ~/.claude/ is a real directory (repair_mutable_agent_dir converts it), so stow
# traverses into it and hits this symlink. ductor_bot manages skill-creator directly.
^/\.claude/skills/skill-creator(/|$)
